.lua
book.chapter(8, "Sections, pipelines, and composition")
.endlua
.sh 2 "An operator can become a function"
.pp
A section captures the missing argument of an operator expression. (+ 1)
increments its input and (* 2) doubles it. Parenthesizing an operator alone,
as in (+), produces its curried function form. This makes operators useful
arguments to folds and maps without inventing trivial named wrappers. The
parser elaborates sections before type checking; the resulting values follow
ordinary function rules.
.lua
book.code("metaml", [=[increment := (+ 1)
double := (* 2)
Test.equal "sections" (increment 4, double 4) (5, 8)
Test.equal "operator as function" ((+) 20 22) 42
Test.equal "operator in fold" (List.fold_left (+) 0 [1, 2, 3]) 6]=],
    "Sections and operator references")
.endlua
.pp
Explicit section holes make argument order visible. (#2 - #1) constructs a
two-argument function that subtracts its first argument from its second.
Repeated holes reuse a parameter, and the highest number determines arity.
As with tacit parameters, indices are positive and bounded. The enclosing
parenthesized section is the binding context; holes do not become global
variables or refer to results from earlier expressions.
.lua
book.code("metaml", [=[reverse_subtract := (#2 - #1)
square_section := (#1 * #1)
Test.equal "reordered operands" (reverse_subtract 3 10) 7
Test.equal "repeated hole" (square_section 6) 36]=], "Local section holes")
.endlua
.sh 2 "Pipelines pass a value"
.pp
The expression x |> f supplies x to f. With data-last APIs, partially apply
the configuration arguments and leave the data argument for the pipeline.
List.map increment is a function awaiting a list; String.split comma is a
function awaiting text. Read a pipeline from left to right as a sequence of
interfaces. Each stage's output type must satisfy the next stage's input type.
.lua
book.code("metaml", [=[total :=
  [1, 2, 3, 4]
  |> List.filter (fn x -> x % 2 == 0)
  |> List.map (* 10)
  |> List.sum
Test.equal "configured stages" total 60]=], "A data-last collection pipeline")
.endlua
.pp
A pipeline is not automatically lazy, streaming, or fused. In the example,
filter constructs a list, map constructs another list, and sum reduces it.
For small data the clarity is often worth those intermediate structures.
For large data a fold can combine the operations in one traversal. The language
does not promise that a visually compact pipeline eliminates allocation or
invokes an optimizer. Performance reasoning must follow the actual operations.
.sh 2 "Composition builds a function"
.pp
Forward composition f >> g means first f and then g. Backward composition
g << f expresses the same order. The Unicode composition spelling is backward
composition as well. Unlike a value pipeline, composition produces a function
that can be stored and applied later. This is useful when multiple inputs
should traverse the same configured sequence of transformations.
.lua
book.code("metaml", [=[increment x := x + 1
double x := x * 2
forward := increment >> double
backward := double << increment
Test.equal "composition order" (forward 3, backward 3) (8, 8)
Test.equal "stored pipeline" (List.map forward [1, 2, 3]) [4, 6, 8]]=],
    "Compose once, apply many times")
book.equation('"(A -> B)" " * " "(B -> C)" " -> " "(A -> C)"',
    "(A -> B) and (B -> C) compose to (A -> C)", "The interface law of composition")
.endlua
.pp
The middle type is the connecting contract. If the first function returns
Option Int and the next expects Int, ordinary composition does not remove
the Option layer. Use Option.map or Option.flat_map as appropriate. Likewise,
Result-producing functions require error-aware composition. The wrapper is
information about absence or failure, not noise to be ignored when arranging
a pipeline. Chapter 23 develops those patterns with complete examples.
.sh 2 "Typed juxtaposition and predictability"
.pp
Bare juxtaposition has a type-directed interpretation in MetaML. Compatible
ordinary application is resolved as application; supported function-typed
contexts can resolve as concatenative composition. The checker records its
decision in the AST, and evaluation follows that decision. This is a typed
elaboration mechanism, not untyped concatenation of arbitrary stack operations.
Types and explicit grouping are therefore essential tools for understanding it.
.pp
For a short idiom, juxtaposition can be elegant. For a long program, explicit
operators usually tell the story better. The book uses |> for data flow and
>> for constructing reusable forward pipelines. When maintaining code that
uses implicit composition, inspect #type and #ast before changing order or
adding arguments. An apparently harmless edit can change which application
relationship is compatible, and thus change the interpretation selected by
the checker.
.sh 2 "Refactor without changing observable behavior"
.pp
For pure functions, replacing nested application with an equivalent pipeline
usually exposes the same mathematical computation. With effects, inspect
when each stage is constructed and when its body runs. A partially applied
operation may evaluate effectful configuration expressions immediately.
A composed function delays its transformation bodies until application.
These timing differences matter for output, mutable resources, and callbacks
that consult external state.
.pp
Algebraic identities also need domain assumptions. Function composition is
associative extensionally for suitable pure functions, but rearranging a
numeric expression can change floating-point rounding, and changing a list
pipeline into a fold can change callback order if written carelessly. State
what equivalence you intend: same value, same errors, same output sequence,
or all of these. A test should observe the contract that clients actually rely
on, rather than only the happy-path integer result.
.lua
book.algorithm("Review a pipeline refactoring", {
    "Write the input and output type of every stage.",
    "Check that adjacent types agree, including Option and Result wrappers.",
    "Record when configuration expressions and callbacks run.",
    "Compare output order and failure behavior on boundary inputs.",
    "Measure intermediate allocation if performance motivated the change."
})
.endlua
.sh 2 "Sources and further work"
.pp
The parser's section elaboration and the checker's application/composition
resolution are the authoritative implementation points. Read the portable
List and Option signatures for data-last examples. Build a text pipeline that
splits comma-separated integers and returns an Option total. First write it
with named intermediate values, then with a pipeline. A malformed field should
preserve failure rather than disappear silently. This exercise connects
composition to the information carried by types.
